{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Have you not known.</b> By balanced reasoning, for through absolute proofs the discerning one knows his Creator." "<b>Or have you not heard.</b> That he should believe the words of the discerning ones." "<b>The Elohim of eternity.</b> The Elohim of eternity, and the meaning is: as He was, so He is, and He does not change." "<b>Creator of the ends of the earth.</b> I have already explained in the section of Genesis (Genesis 1:1) that בורא is close to the form of a participle [like גוזר], and the meaning of קצות is the surrounding line, and according to the opinion of the men of understanding, the line is not a body. And since He is HaShem, standing forever, and the earth endures forever, for He constantly keeps it fixed within the spheres, precisely balanced." "<b>He does not grow faint nor grow weary, and there is no searching of His understanding.</b> And so His might and His wisdom never cease." "And some say that נסתרה דרכי is an allusion to the troubles, that Israel will think that HaShem does not know them, or if He knows them He cannot save them."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:17.476254086Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}